  {
   "id": "69VX0lJxBAAJ",
   "from": "NicheMapR",
   "author": "6cec8ea3702ece93",
   "date": "2022-02-07T19:21:23Z",
   "subject": "Re: Simulating cave microclimate",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hi Nicholas,</div><div><br></div><div>Yes it is possible to do this - I have written some code to do this for Burramys (mountain pygmy possum) for Shane Morris which we&#39;ll finalise soon and release.</div><div><br></div><div>All the best,</div><div>Mike<br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Monday, February 7, 2022 at 3:46:28 PM UTC+11 Nicholas wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Mike, that makes sense! One more question. With the endoR function from NicheMapR, is it able to simulate <b>temperature-dependent torpor </b>(or hibernation; i.e., pronounced reduction, but maintained, physiological states like metabolic rate and EWL; see attached image for example) for a small-bodied mammal? For example, I would like to simulate yearly changes in torpor duration and overall energy expenditure under different climate models. During the spring-summer season, the animal does its usual thing, then in autumn-winter, it enters torpor after reaching below a body temperature threshold (e.g., normal body temp reduces by 5°C). Is there a way to simulate this?<div><div><br></div><div><div>I had a look at your paper Kearney (2019) <i>How will snow alter exposure of organisms to cold under climate change</i>, which talks about hibernation cost. But in the methods, the simulation ran for &quot;a hibernating 20 g endotherm at 5 cm depth&quot; and &quot;Basal metabolic rate was adjusted from the expected normothermic value at 37°C&quot;. So it seems that the simulated endotherm was in a hibernating state all year?  </div></div></div><div><br></div><div>Regards,</div><div>Nicholas</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, 7 Feb 2022 at 14:59, NicheMapR &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">nich...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Hi Nicholas,</div><div><br></div><div>The microclimate model assumes the ~2m deep soil temperature is the running mean of the past year of 2m height air temperature records, as a boundary condition. That should be a very good approximation to a cave temperature. But exactly what the temperature and humidity is will depend on how air is flowing through it, presence of water bodies in the cave, etc. It&#39;s one of the rare situations where the standard bioclim mean annual temperature is a very good approximation for the temperature experienced by an organism!</div><div><br></div><div>All the best,<br>Mike<br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Monday, February 7, 2022 at 11:13:16 AM UTC+11 Nicholas wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone,<div>Is there a function in NicheMapR to simulate a hypothetical cave microclimate for a given location?</div><div><br></div><div>For example, lat = -33.818, lon = 150.022</div><div><br></div><div>Regards,</div><div>Nicholas<br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" color=\"#38761d\">Nicholas C. Wu</font></span></b><b style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:7.5pt;color:green;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"> </span></b><font color=\"#444444\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">| </span><span style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">PhD</span></font></p><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\"></span><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial;vertical-align:baseline\"><b><span style=\"color:rgb(68,68,68);border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"1\">Postdoctoral Research Fellow</font></span></b><b style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:x-small\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,sans-serif\"><span></span></span></b></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial;vertical-align:baseline\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"1\"><font color=\"#444444\">Animal Ecology Lab </font><font style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(89,89,89);border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">| </span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(89,89,89)\">Hawkesbury Institute for the Environment</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial;vertical-align:baseline\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"1\"><span style=\"color:rgb(89,89,89);border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Western Sydney University</span><span style=\"border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font color=\"#444444\">, </font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(89,89,89);border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">NSW </span><span style=\"border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm;background-i